          "id": "8a97d71a3a22906f2bc1a4c5d54822b7b20cf19d",
          "message": "[chore] Rename `waiting-for-maintainers` label to `waiting-for-approvers` (#16065)\n\n#### Description\nI think we should change the name of this label, since all maintainers\nare approvers, but not all approvers are maintainers. The `ready to\nmerge` label should generally be meant for maintainers, rather than\n`waiting for maintainers`. In my humble opinion, `waiting for\nmaintainers` isn’t the most accurate name for this label.\n\n**NOTE**: I'm not really sure how much this change makes sense here (as\ncompared to contrib), as almost everyone is either an approver or\nmaintainer. But I think keeping the same consistency between contrib and\ncore makes this PR worthwhile. Also, this PR is a mirror of this [PR\n](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector-contrib/pull/51654)in\nthe contrib project.\n\n#### Authorship\n\n- [x] I, a human, wrote this pull request description myself.\n\nSigned-off-by: singhvibhanshu <find.vibhanshu@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Alex Boten <223565+codeboten@users.noreply.github.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-10-01T15:51:35Z",
