          "distinct": false,
          "id": "30add0562534958c3b4173fa307b5a3497d0bc9c",
          "message": "[chore] Add section about experimental fields on stable configuration structs (#16214)\n\n<!--Ex. Fixing a bug - Describe the bug and how this fixes the issue.\nEx. Adding a feature - Explain what this achieves.-->\n#### Description\n\nAdds guidance on how to add experimental fields on stable configuration\nstructs. The gist of it is: use a feature gate, think hard about the\nname because there is no going back.\n\nI kept it vague as to when it must fail (unmarshaling vs validation vs\nruntime). I think doing it both at runtime and unmarshaling would be the\nsafest and the most user friendly. I intend to write an mdatagen based\nhelper for this but I want to agree first on this.\n\n<!-- Issue number if applicable -->\n#### Link to tracking issue\n\nThis is an attempt to unblock and set guidance for changes such as\n#16019 and #15212\n\n<!--Authorship attestation. See AGENTS.md for details. AI agents must\nnot check this box on behalf\nof the user; the human author must check it themselves before the PR is\nready for review.-->\n#### Authorship\n\n- [x] I, a human, wrote this pull request description myself.\n\n<!--Please delete paragraphs that you did not use before submitting.-->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Jade Guiton <jade.guiton@datadoghq.com>\nCo-authored-by: Evan Bradley <11745660+evan-bradley@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Alex Boten <223565+codeboten@users.noreply.github.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-10-26T17:41:25Z",
